properties.description:
The guide for running reflow2 from VS Code's Copilot agent where an organisation blocks third-party MCP servers, kept current. Refreshed on 2026-10-05 against main after v0.78.0 (e7e304d), with each command run on a binary built from it. It covers:
- where the door plan stands (steps 1-4 shipped in v0.78.0; step 5, the VS Code setup increment, being built; step 6 planned);
- how to run the door: `reflow2 read` / `reflow2 write`, `--call`, the exit codes, `--describe` and `--list-tools`, the VS Code auto-approve rule for reads, and a user-scope instructions file;
- a measured table and working patterns;
- the limitations that still hold (1, 3's write half, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 15, 20), each with its 2026-10-02 finding;
- what v0.78.0 fixed, the tool frictions and where each stands, and every one of the report's 19 ideas with the record that holds it.
The 2026-10-02 version the triage read is frozen as art:vscode-call-door-field-report-2026-10-02; this file is the living copy and has moved on from it.
